.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "Version 0.4.1" "myutils Library"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "#include \(dqmyfilefunctions.h\(dq"
.sp
.BI "int wordCount(FILE *" file ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR wordCount ()
function reads the file stream pointed to by
.I file
from the beginning, counting the total number of lines, words, and
characters it contains, and stores the results in
.IR lines ", " words ", and " chars
respectively. The file position is rewound before and after the count,
so the function may be called safely regardless of the stream's current
position.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 if
.I file
or any of the output pointers is NULL.
